# tinycmdr repo — what is source and what is per-host state.
#
# Rule: anything a host writes for itself (logs, sessions, memory files, secrets,
# backups) never enters git. One folder goes to six boxes, so a committed per-host
# file would read as canonical and be wrong.

# --- the plan's list (docs/minidsh-hardening-plan.md, stage 1) ---
logs/
sessions/
spill/
state.json
*.bak*
web-token.txt
.env
__pycache__/
dist/
# tools/ is per-host tool payload - with ONE exception: the starter tools
# are shipped source (they ride every package), so they are tracked.
tools/*
!tools/patch.py
!tools/process.py
!tools/toolsmith.py
!tools/README.md
notes.md
atlas.md
knowledge/
skills/.imported-unused/

# --- per-host state and junk the first staging pass found (2026-09-19) ---
# Every name here is a file a host writes for itself, or a scratch artifact.
# Deviations from the plan's list are listed in the stage-1 report.
field-notes.md
# the field-note hit counters: per-host state, written on every failure the harness sees
field-notes-hits.json
notes-archive.md
notes-authored.json
# the confirm gate's approvals (per-host: what the operator told it to stop asking)
confirm-allow.json
tests/eval-runs/
snapshots/
tmp/
uploads/
hermes-tmp/
.archive/
.pre-*
*.pre-*
config.json
jobs.json
inbox/
*.log
# A rotated log keeps a numeric suffix, and `*` stops at the dot: the bot's own tinycmdr.log.1
# (5 MB, rotated 2026-09-30 00:08) showed up as untracked, so `git add -A` in a live tree would
# have committed a host log. Both names belong here for the same reason.
*.log.*
*.lock
*.tmp
skills/
.env.*
!.env.example
web-token.txt.*
web-sessions.json
# the tools/ provenance record written at run start (ToolRegistry.note_provenance)
tools-provenance.json
a.txt
lines.txt*

# Internal fleet operational tooling & notes
maintenance/atlas-notes/
# Our own engineering notes: they name hosts, addresses and the operator's
# decisions, so they are never shipped and never committed.
docs/dev-log.md
docs/deferred-corrections.md
maintenance/fleet-version-report.ps1
maintenance/fleet-metrics.py
maintenance/register-boot-recovery.ps1
maintenance/start-containers.ps1
maintenance/task-audit.ps1
maintenance/restart-tinycmdr-the manager box.ps1
docs/handoff-*.md
docs/staged-*.md
# The pre-edit copy of the build the batch is graded against (A/A): it is a whole
# build, not source, so it is a scratch artifact.
probe-pre.py
launch_tinycmdr.bat
tinycmdr-service.vbs

# The fleet's private inventory (host names, ids, addresses, secret labels).
# build-package.py refuses to build a public package without it.
maintenance/private_rules.py

# maintenance/where.py's per-host tree declaration: it names this box's own paths
# (a backup share, an ops workspace), which are true of one machine and nobody else.
maintenance/where-roles.json

# --- found by adopting the git path on the fleet (2026-09-24): every host showed these
# as untracked, which makes `git status` useless for spotting real drift.
venv/
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
# --- found on the live box (2026-09-29) by maintenance/where.py, for the same reason ---
# experiments.jsonl is written by the run itself; the tool-audit folder is one box's
# evidence dump. Neither is source, and both made `git status` in the live tree look
# dirty next to a REAL tracked modification - the two are now told apart.
experiments.jsonl
maintenance/tool-audit-*/
